1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,509
On July 7th, 1881, the steamer Proteus sailed from St. John's, Newfoundland, and turned north toward Greenland.

2
00:00:09,509 --> 00:00:13,424
On board was Lieutenant Adolphus Greely's expedition.

3
00:00:13,425 --> 00:00:19,206
On August 11th, she anchored in Discovery Harbor, on Lady Franklin Bay.

4
00:00:19,206 --> 00:00:22,096
Eight days later, the Proteus left.

5
00:00:22,096 --> 00:00:24,023
Twenty-five men stayed behind.

6
00:00:24,025 --> 00:00:27,189
A relief ship was sent in 1882.

7
00:00:27,189 --> 00:00:29,449
The Neptune never reached them.

8
00:00:29,450 --> 00:00:34,256
In 1883, a second relief expedition went north on the Proteus.

9
00:00:34,256 --> 00:00:39,499
On July 23rd, she was crushed in the pack ice and sank.

10
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:47,218
On June 22nd, 1884, the ships Thetis and Bear found seven men alive near Cape Sabine.

11
00:00:47,218 --> 00:00:50,594
Seventeen had starved, and one had drowned.

12
00:00:50,594 --> 00:00:52,523
Only six came home.

